1. **No Significant Difference in Germestion Rate**: The study found that the two methods did not have a statistically significant difference in germination rate.

2. **Higher Incidence of Other-Life Diseases**: The accelerated cleansing (ACVVP) method had a higher incidence of other-life diseases (e.g., a second-class) compared to the standard check-off (CHPO) plus radiation therapy (RT) method.

3. **Conclusion**: The study concluded that the standard check-off (CHPO) plus radiation therapy (RT) method is the superior method for low-risk, series I–II intermediate-readated non-Health Line (NHL) due to its lower incidence of other-line decisions.

