","When \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas is passed into a mixture of \( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \texttext{Ni}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) ions in an acidified aqueous solution, the following products are expected:

1. **\( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) in acidic solution**: The reaction is:
   \[
   \text{M}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S} \rightarrow \text{M}^{2+} + \text{H}_2\text{S}
   \]
   The solubility of metal sulfides depends on the hardness of the metal. The higher the hardness, the more stable the sulfide is.

2. **Solability of metal sulfides**:
   - **\( \text{Mn}^{2+} \):** Forms \( \text{MnS} \). \( \text{MnS} \) is insoluble in water and precipitates.
   - **\( \text{Ni}^{2+} \):** Forms \( \text{NiS} \). \( \text{NiS \) is insoluble in water and precipitates.
   - **\( \text{Cu}^{2+} \):** Forms \( \text{CuS} \). \( \text{CuS} \) is insoluble in water and precipitates.
   - **\( \text{Hg}^{2+} \):** Forms \( \text{HgS} \). \( \text{HgS} \) is insoluble in water and precipitates.

3. **Conclusion**:
   All the metal sulfides (\( \text{MnS} \), \( \text{NiS} \), \( \text{CuS} \), and \( \text{HgS} \)) are insoluble in water and precipitate upon the addition of \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas.

Thus, the sulfides precipitated are:
- \( \text{MnS} \)
- \( \text{NiS \)
- \( \text{CuS} \)
- \( \text{HgS} \)

