   The cell reaction is the combination of the reduction and oxidation half-reactions:
   - Oxidation: \( \text{Cu} \rightarrow \text{Cu}^{2+} + 2e^- \quad \text{(at the cathode)} \)
   - Reduction: \( \text{Ag}^{2+} + 2e^- \rightarrow \text{Ag} \quad \text{(at the cathode)} \)
   The overall cell reaction is:
   \[
   \text{Cu} + \text{Ag}^{2+} \rightarrow \text{Cu}^{2+} + \text{Ag}
   \]

2. **Calculate the standard cell potential (E°)**:
   \[
   E° = E^\circ_{\text{Ag}^{2+}/Ag} - E^\circ_{\text{Cu}^{2+}/Cu} = 0.7996 \, \text{V} - 0.342 \, \text{V} = 0.4576 \, \text{V}
   \]

