   \]
   \[
   E = 0.4576 \, \text{V} - 0.000203 \times 0.693 = 0.4576 \, \text{V} - 0.000140 = 0.45746 \, \text{V}
   \]

4. **Calculate the polarization**:
   \[
   \text{Polarration} = E - E^\circ = 0.45746 \, \text{V} - 0.4576 \, \text{V} = -0.00014 \, \text{V}
   \]

