For a coaxial cable, the electric and magnetic fields are:
\[
\mathbf{E} = \frac{\xi}{2\pi r} \left( \frac{1}{r} \text{ for } 0 < r < a, \quad \frac{1}{a} \text{ for } a < r < b, \quad 0 \text{ for } r > b \right) \hat{z}
