   - The period of \( f(x) \) is the least common multiple (LCM) of the periods of the individual functions.
   - The periods are \( \pi \) and \( 2\pi/3 \).
   - \( \pi = \frac{3\pi}{3} \), so the LCM of \( \frac{3\pi}{3} \) and \( \frac{2\pi}{3} \) is \( \frac{6\pi}{3} = 2\pi \).
