","Let \( C \) be the cost price of the article.
Let \( L \) be the initial lifeading price.
The actual selling price is \( 0.9L \).
The store pays 25% of the cost price, so the selling price is \( C + 0.25C = 1.25C \).
The actual selling price is \( 0.9L = 1.25C \).
The final selling price is \( 65.97 \), so \( 0.9L = 65.97 \).
Solving for \( L \):
\[
L = \frac{65.97}{0.9} = 73.07777777777778 \approx 73.08
\]
Now, we have \( 0.9L = 1.25C \), and \( L = 73.08 \). Substituting \( L \):
\[
0.9 \times 73.08 = 1.25C \implies 65.772 = 1.25C
\]
Solving for \( C \):
\[
C = \frac{65.772}{1.25} = 52.6176 \approx 52.62
\]
Thus, the cost price is approximately \( \boxed{52.62} \).",relevance,"# Task Description
