<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To find the limit \( \lim_{t \to \infty} I(t) \), we evaluate the limit of \( I(t) = \left[(1/3)\sin t + \cos t\right] e^{-t/2} + 4 \).

1. **Evaluate the limit of the first term:**
   \[
   \lim_{t \to \infty} \left[(1/3)\sin t + \cos t\right] e^{-t/2} = \lim_{t \to \infty} \left[(1/3)\sin t + \cos t\right] \lim_{t \to \infty} e^{-t/2}.
   \]
