","To solve the system of linear equations, we solve the system:
\[
\begin{align*} 
x + ky + 3z &= 0 \quad \text{(1)} \\ 
x + ky - 2z &= 0 \quad \text{(2)} \\ 
2x + 4y - 3z &= 0 \quad \text{(3)} 
\end{align*} 
\]
Subtracting (2) from (1), we get:
\[
(x + ky + 3z) - (x + ky - 2z) = 0 \implies 5z = 0 \implies z = 0.
\]
Substituting \( z = 0 \) into the equations, we get:
\[
\begin{align*} 
x + ky &= 0 \quad \text{(4)} \\ 
2x + 4y &= 0 \quad \text{(5)} 
\end{align*} 
\]
From (4), \( x = -ky \). Substituting into (5), we get:
\[
2(-ky) + 4y = 0 \implies -2ky + 4y = 0 \implies y(4 - 2k) = 0.
\]
For a non-zero solution \((x, y, z)\), we must have \( y \neq 0 \), so \( 4 - 2k = 0 \), which implies \( k = 2 \). 

