## CONVERSATION

<USER_REQUEST>
State whether each study is cross-sectional, retrospective, or prospective.  

a) To see if there is a link between smoking and bladder cancer, patients with bladder cancer are asked if they currently smoke or if they smoked in the past.  
b) The Nurses Health Survey was a survey where nurses were asked to record their eating habits over a period of time, and their general health was recorded.  
c) A new study is underway to track the eating and exercise patterns of people at different time-periods in the future, and see who is afflicted with cancer later in life.  
d) The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
a) **Retemporressive**: This is a retrospective study because the study asks people to look in the past (e.g., ""Did they previously smoked?"") to determine if they were already in the future (e.g., ""They have backward-temporal nature"").  

b) **Cross-sequential**: The NHS is a continuous timeline of events, so it is a cross-sequential study.  

c) **Prospective**: This is a prospective study because the study starts now and will look into the future to see if eating and exercise patterns influence future cancer outcomes.  

d) **Cross-sectional**: This is a cross-sequential study because it compares two events at the same time (e.g., ""The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items."")
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

