1. **Definition of Riemann-Liouville Fractional Derivative:**
   The Riemann-Liouville fractional derivative \( aD_t^P f(t) \) is defined as:
   \[
   aD_t^P f(t) = \frac{1}{a} \int_0^t \frac{f(t_0)}{(t - t_0)^{P+1}} \, dt_0.
   \]
   where \( P > 0 \) and \( a \) is a constant.

2. **Calculation of \( aD_t^p (aD_t^q f(t)) \):**
   \[
   aD_t^p (aD_t^q f(t)) = \frac{1}{a} \int_0^t \frac{aD_t^q f(t_0)}{(t - t_0)^{p+1}} \, dt_0.
   \]
   Substituting the definition of \( aD_t^q f(t_0) \):
   \[
   aD_t^p (aD_t^q f(t)) = \frac{1}{a} \int_0^t \frac{1}{a} \int_0^t_0 \frac{f(t_0)}{(t_0 - t_0)^q+1} \, dt_0 \, \frac{1}{(t - t_0)^{p+1}} \, dt_0.
   \]
