A probability law $\mathbb{P}$ is a mathematical framework that assigns probabilities to possible outcomes of a random event. It is a mathematical model that describes the likelihood of various outcomes occurring in a random event. The term "" probability law"" is often used as an synonym for ""probability distribution"" or ""probability measure.""
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

