You’re pulling a chest of drawers, applying a force of 60.0 N at an angle of 60.0°. How much work do you do pulling it over 10.0 m?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the work done, we use the formula:  
\[ W = F \cdot d \cdot \cos \theta \]  
where:  
- \( F = 60.0 \, \text{N} \) (force applied),  
- \( d = 10.0 \, \text{m} \) (displacement),  
- \( \theta = 60.0° \) (angle between the force and displacement).  

Substituting the values:  
\[ W = 60.0 \, \text{N} \cdot 10.0 \, \text{m} \cdot \cos 60.0° \]  
\[ W = 600 \, \text{N} \cdot \text{m} \cdot 0.5 \]  
\[ W = 300 \, \text{J} \]  

Thus, the work done is \(\boxed{300 \, \text{J}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

